<v Judy>来吧。走。

00:49:38.080 --> 00:50:05.430
<v Zoe Chace>We try a couple more spots. We slip into a construction site through a gap in the fence. To me, as a New Yorker, this feels very wrong. Like, you don't go to these places in the city, because rats. They have their corners of the city. We have ours. They are in the subway tracks. We are on the platform. They're in the shadows, and we stay in the lights. It feels physically hard to force myself into this territory.
<v Zoe Chace>我们试了几个更多的地方。我们通过围栏上的缝隙滑进了一个建筑工地。对我来说，作为一个纽约人，这感觉非常不对。就像，你不会去城里这些地方，因为老鼠。它们有它们在城市的角落。我们有我们的。它们在地铁轨道里。我们在站台上。它们在阴影里，我们待在光里。强迫自己进入这个领土感觉身体上很难受。

00:50:05.430 --> 00:50:08.630
<v Zoe Chace>I want to die. I want to die.
<v Zoe Chace>我想死。我想死。

00:50:08.630 --> 00:50:09.940
<v Susan>Catcher is carrying around a dead rat.
<v Susan>捕获者正带着一只死老鼠到处走。

00:50:09.940 --> 00:50:10.850
<v Zoe Chace>Where are we? What is this?
<v Zoe Chace>我们在哪？这是什么？

00:50:10.850 --> 00:50:17.750
<v Judy>We're in some kind of an enclosure. It's really smelly and dirty.
<v Judy>我们处在某种围栏里。这真的很臭很脏。

00:50:17.750 --> 00:50:26.470
<v Richard>Freeze. Everybody freeze. Freeze. Hold Ray right there. There's a rat ready to come out.
<v Richard>冻住。所有人冻住。冻住。就在那里抓住雷。有只老鼠准备出来。

00:50:26.470 --> 00:50:30.910
<v Zoe Chace>Ray sniffs around haphazardly. Here's his mic.
<v Zoe Chace>雷漫无目的地四处嗅。这是他的麦克风。

00:50:30.910 --> 00:50:32.000
<v Zoe Chace>[PANTING]
<v Zoe Chace>[喘气声]

00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:32.800
<v Zoe Chace>Looks up at Judy.
<v Zoe Chace>抬头看朱迪。

00:50:32.800 --> 00:50:35.750
<v Judy>I think he's done.
<v Judy>我觉得他完成了。

00:50:35.750 --> 00:50:36.580
<v Zoe Chace>What did he do?
<v Zoe Chace>他做了什么？

00:50:36.580 --> 00:50:45.000
<v Judy>Nothing. He's looking for food. He's not looking for rats. Oh my god.
<v Judy>什么也没做。他在找食物。他不在找老鼠。天哪。

00:50:45.000 --> 00:51:15.550
<v Zoe Chace>But then we come to this dark alley. And this time, they specifically set it up for Ray to make a kill. Judy and Ray Ray stay just inside the alleyway. Behind us, there's a guy peeing into a dumpster. At the end of the alley is one of the dog owners, Susan. She looks so out of place. She's in shorts, white running shoes, standing in the middle of a pile of garbage, poking at it with sticks. She's trying to flush out a rat for her dog to catch. Judy, Ray, and I just watch.
<v Zoe Chace>但后来我们来到这个黑暗的小巷。这一次，他们专门为雷设置了一个捕杀。朱迪和雷雷就待在巷子里。我们后面，有个家伙正对着垃圾箱撒尿。巷子的尽头是其中一个狗主人，苏珊。她看起来太不搭调了。她穿着短裤，白跑鞋，站在一堆垃圾中间，用棍子捅它们。她正试图把老鼠冲出来让她的狗抓。朱迪、雷和我只是看着。

00:51:15.550 --> 00:51:17.780
<v Zoe Chace>See, she really gets in the garbage over there.
<v Zoe Chace>看，她真的钻进那边的垃圾里。

00:51:17.780 --> 00:51:23.650
<v Judy>Yeah. She's good. She really entertains her dog.
<v Judy>是的。她很好。她真的取悦了她的狗。

00:51:23.650 --> 00:51:33.160
<v Zoe Chace>We're just seeing this so differently. Judy is thinking, that's amazing. I'm thinking, that's disgusting. Here's how Ray's feeling as he's watching.
<v Zoe Chace>我们看到的太不一样了。朱迪心想，那太棒了。我心想，那太恶心了。这是雷在看的时候的感觉。

00:51:33.160 --> 00:51:37.460
<v Zoe Chace>[WHINING]
<v Zoe Chace>[呜呜声]

00:51:37.460 --> 00:51:46.090
<v Zoe Chace>No rats run our way, so Judy decides, screw the battle plan. She's going to let Ray off leash, and tears off to find the other dogs in the garbage pile.
<v Zoe Chace>没有老鼠跑向我们，所以朱迪决定，去他的战斗计划。她要放开雷，冲去垃圾堆里找其他狗。

00:51:46.090 --> 00:51:56.220
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>One rat emerges from the scrum and runs under a stack of loose boards next to the sidewalk. Ray heads in after it. This is the sound of him banging his head and paws under those boards.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>一只老鼠从混战中跑出来，跑到人行道旁边的一堆松动的木板下。雷追在后面。这是他撞头和爪子撞那些木板的声音。

00:51:56.220 --> 00:51:57.060
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>[POUNDING]
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>[撞击声]

00:51:57.060 --> 00:51:58.300
<v Susan>Come on, Tanner. Go around.
<v Susan>来吧，坦纳。绕过去。

00:51:58.300 --> 00:52:00.770
<v Susan>[SCURRYING]
<v Susan>[奔跑声]

00:52:00.770 --> 00:52:01.700
<v Susan>[SQUEAKING]
<v Susan>[吱吱声]

00:52:01.700 --> 00:52:04.040
<v Judy>Get 'em! Get 'em! Get 'em!
<v Judy>去抓它们！去！去！

00:52:04.040 --> 00:52:33.600
<v Zoe Chace>I'm just going to pause things for a moment here, because what happened next goes really fast. And amazingly, we actually have a picture of this exact moment that Bill took with some kind of high-speed camera. The picture shows two dogs, Paco, Ray, and one very large New York City rat. The rat looks like it's doing some move from The Matrix , like slow-motion flying through the air, twisting at the waist, right across Paco's face, trying to escape his assailants. And then--
<v Zoe Chace>我在这里暂停一下，因为接下来发生的事非常快。而且令人惊奇的是，我们确实有比尔用某种高速摄像机拍到的这个精确时刻的照片。照片显示了两只狗，帕科、雷和一只非常大的纽约市老鼠。那只老鼠看起来像是在做黑客帝国里的动作，就像慢动作飞过空中，腰部扭转，穿过帕科的脸，试图逃离攻击者。然后——

00:52:33.600 --> 00:52:34.520
<v Zoe Chace>[SCREAMING]
<v Zoe Chace>[尖叫声]

00:52:34.520 --> 00:52:35.440
<v Susan>[INAUDIBLE] Tanner!
<v Susan>[听不清]坦纳！

00:52:35.440 --> 00:52:44.320
<v Richard>Good. Good. Good! Good! Good boy! Judith, wonderful.
<v Richard>好。好。好！好！好孩子！朱迪丝，太棒了。

00:52:44.320 --> 00:52:52.750
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>Ray doesn't kill the rat. He misses him. But he pushes the rat right into Paco's face. I'm going to give Ray Ray an assist on this one.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>雷没杀死那只老鼠。他错过了。但他把老鼠正好推进了帕科的脸。我会给雷雷助攻一个。

00:52:52.750 --> 00:52:53.690
<v Zoe Chace>You did it, Ray.
<v Zoe Chace>你做到了，雷。

00:52:53.690 --> 00:52:54.690
<v Susan>Yeah! Woo!
<v Susan>耶！呜！

00:52:54.690 --> 00:52:57.690
<v Judy>Yay! Can we go home now?
<v Judy>耶！我们可以回家了吗？

00:52:57.690 --> 00:52:59.210
<v Susan>Leave it, Tanner.
<v Susan>离开它，坦纳。

00:52:59.210 --> 00:53:07.210
<v Richard>Tally-ho! Tally-ho. He wants back in. He's going after him. He's got the gene turned on now.
<v Richard>看哪！看哪。他想要回去。他正追着它。他现在把基因开启了。

00:53:07.210 --> 00:53:12.530
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>Ray's passed the test. He's a hunter. He circles back to the blood on the sidewalk.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>雷通过了测试。他是个猎人。他转回人行道上的血迹。

00:53:12.530 --> 00:53:15.510
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>Oh, wow. That's-- he's licking the blood.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>哦，哇。那是——他正在舔血。

00:53:15.510 --> 00:53:24.740
<v Judy>Yuck! Don't drink the blood.
<v Judy>呕！别喝血。

00:53:24.740 --> 00:53:36.800
<v Zoe Chace>I saw this quote in an article about terriers from the poet A. E. Housman. "I can no more define poetry than a terrier can define a rat." Ray has found his poetry.
<v Zoe Chace>我在诗人A·E·豪斯曼关于梗犬的文章里看到过这句引语。“我可以定义诗歌，就像梗犬可以定义老鼠一样。”雷已经找到了他的诗。

00:53:36.800 --> 00:53:45.190
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>Judy puts Ray back on the leash. She seems a little shaken up, and she's ready to leave the Ryders Alley Trencher-Fed Society and go home.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>朱迪把雷放回皮带上。她看起来有点震惊，她准备离开莱德胡同挖掘喂养协会回家。

00:53:45.190 --> 00:53:55.200
<v Judy>I'm dirty. I'm smelly. I'm tired. I'm thirsty. Now I have to give my dog a bath. I want to get home and wash my hands.
<v Judy>我脏了。我很臭。我很累。我很渴。现在我得给我的狗洗澡。我想回家洗手。

00:53:55.200 --> 00:54:00.430
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>Judy and little Ray Ray get in a taxi back to their apartment. Richard says he's seen her kind before.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>朱迪和小雷雷乘出租车回到他们的公寓。理查德说他以前见过她那样的人。

00:54:00.430 --> 00:54:10.150
<v Richard>I doubt she'll be back, but you never know. We get a lot of people like that who come, whose dogs show promise, but you can tell that they don't have the--
<v Richard>我怀疑她不会回来了，但你永远不知道。我们有很多那样的人，他们的狗表现出希望，但你能看出他们没有——

00:54:10.150 --> 00:54:13.170
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>It's like their dog has the instinct, but they don't.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>就像他们的狗有本能，但他们没有。

00:54:13.170 --> 00:54:27.800
<v Richard>Well, I don't think she's a hunter. The dog is much more of a hunter than she is.
<v Richard>嗯，我不觉得她是猎人。狗比她更像猎人。

00:54:27.800 --> 00:54:54.110
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>A few days later, Judy emailed us that Ray wasn't playing with his toys. I've been worried about this-- that there would be some irrevocable change in him. After tasting blood, his squeaky ball would just seem pathetic. But a few days later, he was back to his toys and Judy and Ray are going rat hunting again. This surprised me. It makes him happy, she said. She wants him to be happy.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>几天后，朱迪发邮件告诉我们雷不玩他的玩具了。我一直为此担心——会有某种他不可挽回的改变。尝过血后，他的尖叫球会显得很可悲。但几天后，他又回到了他的玩具里，朱迪和雷又去捕鼠了。这让我惊讶。这让他开心，她说。她希望他开心。

00:54:54.110 --> 00:55:16.220
<v Zoe Chace>When he and Judy walk down the street now, they are having exactly opposite experiences. I imagine what's in Ray's head as this X-ray version of New York City. Legions of rats running just under the sidewalks, in every courtyard, behind every stack of garbage. When he smells the air that comes out of the subway, he knows they're there.
<v Zoe Chace>当他和朱迪现在走在街上时，他们有着截然不同的体验。我想象雷脑海里那个X射线版本的纽约市。成群的老鼠跑在人行道下，在每个庭院，在每堆垃圾后面。当他闻到从地铁里出来的空气时，他知道它们在那里。

00:55:16.220 --> 00:55:40.440
<v Zoe Chace>Judy, meanwhile, like all New Yorkers, lives surrounded by rats and tries her best to pretend they're not here. But for Ray, she'll cross over, look at the world as a terrier might, the same way you see couples walking down the streets of New York, hand-in-hand, one suffering through something the other one needs, just in order to feel like themselves.
<v Zoe Chace>朱迪，同时，像所有纽约人一样，生活在老鼠的包围中，尽量假装它们不存在。但为了雷，她会跨过界，像梗犬那样看世界，就像你看到情侣走在纽约街头，手牵手，一个忍受着另一个所需要的东西，只是为了感觉像他们自己。

00:55:40.440 --> 00:55:44.340
<v Ira Glass>Zoe Chace and Emmanuel Dzotsi are producers on our show.
<v Ira Glass>佐伊·蔡斯和伊曼纽尔·佐齐是我们节目的制作人。

00:55:44.340 --> 00:56:13.290
<v Ira Glass>[MUSIC - "I SMELL A RAT" BY BIG MAMA THORNTON]
<v Ira Glass>[音乐 - 大妈妈索顿的《I SMELL A RAT》]

00:56:13.290 --> 00:56:26.930
<v Ira Glass>[MUSIC - "THE 5TH QUARTER" BY THE MADHATTERS]
<v Ira Glass>[音乐 - 疯帽子乐队的《THE 5TH QUARTER》]

00:56:26.930 --> 00:56:38.880
<v Ira Glass>Our program was produced today by Stephanie Foo. Our production staff, Zoe Chace, Dana Chivvas, Sean Cole, Neil Drumming, Karen Duffin, Emmanuel Dzotsi, David Kestenbaum, Chana Joffe-Walt, Miki Meek, Jonathan Menjivar, Robyn Semien, Matt Tierney, and Nancy Updike.
<v Ira Glass>我们的节目今天由斯蒂芬妮·福制作。我们的制作人员，佐伊·蔡斯、达纳·奇瓦斯、肖恩·科尔、尼尔·德拉明、凯伦·达芬、伊曼纽尔·佐齐、大卫·凯斯滕鲍姆、查纳·乔夫-沃尔特、米基·米克、乔纳森·门吉瓦尔、罗宾·塞米恩、马特·蒂尔尼和南希·厄普戴克。

00:56:38.880 --> 00:56:48.450
<v Ira Glass>Editing help from Susan Burton, Julie Snyder, and Elna Baker. Our digital staff, Whitney Dangerfield and Julie Whitaker. Research help today from Christopher Swetala. Music help from Damien Graef and Rob Geddis.
<v Ira Glass>苏珊·伯顿、朱莉·斯奈德和埃尔娜·贝克的编辑帮助。我们的数字员工，惠特尼·丹格菲尔德和朱莉·惠特克。今天的研究帮助来自克里斯托弗·斯韦塔拉。达米安·格拉夫和罗布·格迪斯的音乐帮助。

00:56:48.450 --> 00:57:03.580
<v Ira Glass>[ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS]
<v Ira Glass>[致谢]

00:57:03.580 --> 00:57:11.900
